<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17411" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλέω</span></b> , 
			Boeot.
		
		part.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					7.3211
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				3212
			</span></i> (Orchom. 
				Boeot.
			): (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλός</span>):—<i>play
				on the flute,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φρύγιον αὔλησεν μέλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alcm.
					82
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.141
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.60
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				327a
			</span></i>: c. dat. pers., <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				2.8
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐ. ἔξοδον</span>
			<i>play</i> a finale, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				582
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐ. εἰρεσίαν,</span> of the
			boatswain, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				2
			</span></i>:— 
				Pass.
			, of tunes, <i>to be played on the flute,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ Βακχεῖος ῥυθμὸς ηὐλεῖτο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					9.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλεῖται πᾶν μέλαθρον</span>”
				<i>is filled with music,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IT</u>
					367
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of persons,
				<i>play to,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VA</u>
				2.34
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Synt.</u>
				302.1
			</span></i>:—mostly in 
				Pass.
			, <i>to be played to, hear music,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				6.1.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				4.5.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				917b19
			</span></i> (but possibly 
				Med.
			 as in <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				791a
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Char.</u>
				19.10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				20.10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> generally,
				<i>play,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέρατι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>DDeor.</u>
					12.1
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				4.74
			</span></i>.</div>
